From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: uxtheme, win32u: dark mode follows the app mode, live, in every program

Settings' "Choose your default app mode" writes HKCU\...\Themes\Personalize
AppsUseLightTheme and broadcasts WM_SETTINGCHANGE "ImmersiveColorSet"; on
Windows every program's controls, and the system colours, follow. Here:

- uxtheme: RefreshImmersiveColorPolicyState (ordinal 104, was a stub) selects
  the active style's "Dark" colour scheme while AppsUseLightTheme is 0 and its
  default scheme otherwise (a style without Dark is left alone). Only the
  scheme's system colours are applied (SetSysColors, and HKCU\Control
  Panel\Colors so they persist) -- never its fonts or sizes, which are the
  user's. ColorName is written, WM_THEMECHANGED goes to every window, and
  every shown, framed window repaints its frame. The shell calls it (0163).
- uxtheme: a process follows a switch made by another: the ThemeManager key
  is watched (RegNotifyChangeKeyValue), and OpenThemeData/IsThemeActive load
  the new scheme -- controls reopen their theme data on WM_THEMECHANGED.
  Stock Wine loaded the style once, at DLL load.
- win32u: a process reads the system colours again when another process
  broadcasts WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE (each process cached them at first use, so
  SetSysColors reached only its caller). A changed colour gets a new brush and
  pen; the old ones stay valid for programs holding them.

Gate: test/darkmode-gate.sh.
